---
import LegalPage from '../layouts/LegalPage.astro'
import { LEGAL_ENTITY, draftPending, isPlaceholder } from '@shared/legal'

// Highlight a detail only while THAT detail is still a placeholder. A page-wide
// flag would mark a filled field as pending the moment any other one wasn't.
const ph = (value: string) => (isPlaceholder(value) ? 'placeholder' : undefined)

// Name every field this page publishes that the shared identity check does
// not already cover. Leave one out and the banner can go while that field
// is still a token.
const draft = draftPending(LEGAL_ENTITY.governingLaw)
---
<LegalPage title="Terms of Service">
  {draft && (
    <div class="draft-banner">
      <strong>Draft</strong> — this notice is not final. Some details of the operator are
      still to be confirmed, and this banner disappears once they are.
    </div>
  )}

  <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
  <p class="meta">Last updated: 2026-11-27</p>

  <p>
    Cire is a digital wedding invitation and wedding planning service. Couples and the people
    helping them plan use the organiser portal at host.cireweddings.com, their guests use the
    invitation site at invite.cireweddings.com, wedding suppliers use the vendor portal at
    vendor.cireweddings.com, and this site, cireweddings.com, describes the service. It is
    operated by <span class={ph(LEGAL_ENTITY.name)}>{LEGAL_ENTITY.name}</span>, trading as Cire
    (&ldquo;Cire&rdquo;, &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;). By creating a wedding or a vendor
    listing, or otherwise using the service, you agree to these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Who can use Cire</h2>
  <p>
    You must be 18 or older to organise a wedding on Cire or to run a vendor listing. Guests use
    the invitation their couple sends them under the separate terms shown on the invitation site.
  </p>

  <h2>The service</h2>
  <p>
    Cire lets couples and their organisers create wedding invitations, collect RSVPs, and plan their
    wedding. Guests use the invitation site with a code supplied by their couple; organisers and
    vendors sign in with a Musubi account.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <p>
    Keep your sign-in method secure — you are responsible for activity under your account. Provide
    accurate information and keep it up to date.
  </p>

  <h2>Plans</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The free plan, Ivory, includes the invitation, the guest list, RSVPs and guest import, for
      up to 100 guests.</li>
    <li>The paid plans, Gold and Crimson, are <strong>one-time purchases that apply to a single
      wedding</strong>. What each includes, and its price, is set out under
      <a href="/#pricing">Pricing</a>. A plan is not transferable between weddings or accounts.</li>
    <li>Once you have bought a plan for a wedding, we will not take it back, except when we refund
      the purchase.</li>
    <li>We may change what each plan includes for weddings that buy it later.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Purchases and payment</h2>
  <p>
    You buy a plan from us. Stripe takes the payment on our behalf, and we never see your card
    details. Prices include GST. If you need a tax invoice, ask us at
    <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_ENTITY.supportEmail}`}><span class={ph(LEGAL_ENTITY.supportEmail)}>{LEGAL_ENTITY.supportEmail}</span></a>. Refunds are
    handled under our <a href="/refunds/">Refund Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your content and your guests&rsquo; information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You keep ownership of everything you upload — invitation wording, images, schedules, guest
      lists. You grant us the licence needed to host, display and process it solely to provide the
      service.</li>
    <li>When you upload guest information (names, contact details, dietary needs), you confirm you
      are entitled to share it with us for managing your wedding. We handle it on your behalf as
      described in our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Notice</a>, and we never sell it, advertise
      against it or profile anyone with it. Three decisions are ours rather than yours, because
      we make them the same way for every wedding: the retention window, the security of the
      service, and the technical telemetry it emits.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Vendor listings</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>If you run a listing, you are responsible for what it says being accurate and yours to
      publish.</li>
    <li>A listing a couple created can be claimed by the business it names. We check a claim
      before we hand the listing over.</li>
    <li>Anything a couple and a vendor agree — a booking, a quote, a payment — is between them. We
      carry the enquiry; we are not a party to the arrangement.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Don&rsquo;t misuse the service — no unlawful content, no attempts to disrupt or gain
    unauthorised access to it, no using it to spam or harass, and no accessing it other than through
    the interfaces we provide.
  </p>

  <h2>Australian Consumer Law</h2>
  <p>
    Our services come with guarantees that cannot be excluded under the Australian Consumer Law.
    Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts or modifies any consumer guarantee, right or remedy
    you have under the Australian Consumer Law or any other law that cannot lawfully be excluded.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, and subject to the consumer guarantees above, our total
    liability in connection with the service is limited to AUD 100, and we are not liable for
    indirect or consequential loss. This limit does not reduce a refund under our
    <a href="/refunds/">Refund Policy</a>. We provide the service with due care and skill but do
    not promise it will be uninterrupted or error-free.
  </p>

  <h2>Ending the service</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using Cire and ask us to delete your wedding data at any time. We may suspend or
    close accounts that seriously or repeatedly breach these terms. If we ever discontinue the
    service, we will give you reasonable notice and a way to export your data.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms from time to time. The &ldquo;last updated&rdquo; date above changes
    when we do, and changes are not retroactive. If you use Cire with a Musubi account and a change
    matters, we also email that account&rsquo;s address before it takes effect, saying what changes
    and from what day.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of <strong>{LEGAL_ENTITY.governingLaw}</strong>, and the
    courts of that state have non-exclusive jurisdiction. This does not deprive you of protections
    you have under the consumer laws of the place where you live.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_ENTITY.supportEmail}`}><span class={ph(LEGAL_ENTITY.supportEmail)}>{LEGAL_ENTITY.supportEmail}</span></a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
